CHANGELOG: the Unreleased block consolidated, and DRACO.md stops calling it stale

Dev asked for a CHANGELOG covering what has been pushed since the previous one. An audit against the
git log found it already did: twenty-five entries across the eighteen substantive commits since the
alpha.6 release, each written with its commit's record as the operating rule requires. What it lacked
was shape. The entries had accumulated newest-first under whichever heading each commit prepended,
which left the block with two "Changed" sections and no way to read it as a whole.

Now one section each — Added, Changed, Fixed, Build — with every entry preserved verbatim and a lead
paragraph naming the arcs: the forest as a corpus, the case body element, Source and Target as roles
with Drake as the Source, generation as a transform, and GenDrake running. One entry carried a claim
the same release later overrode — that Generator is "universal over Sources" — and says so now in
place, rather than being rewritten to look right in hindsight.

DRACO.md §5 said the CHANGELOG "stops at alpha.5"; it has carried alpha.6 and a full Unreleased
block since 8aef403. Corrected in the same commit, as that file's own rule requires.

